[statement]
As `a-condition-forbidding-a-name-the-package-provides-at-no-version-holds`,
the condition holds only once nothing else is left to decide: the `!`
entry admits the package itself, which could still be installed, and
waits for it as for any package it names
(`a-negated-entry-waits-for-the-package-it-names`). `c` needs `e`, and
`e` needs `w`; `s` provides `pv` and `w` at no version, its condition is
`c` and `!pv`, and `wb` provides `w` with a priority. apk decides `w`
first, installing `wb`, and installs `s` after it. Without the `!` entry,
`s` is installed for its condition at once, and answers `w`.

[repository]
P:c
V:2
D:e

P:e
V:2
D:w

P:s
V:1
p:pv w
i:c !pv

P:wb
V:1
k:1
p:w

[request]
c

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install wb 1
install e 2
install c 2
install s 1
